     "hidden": false,
     "text": "What was made and why: Percutaneous implants need a tight skin seal; bare -> Si-substituted hydroxyapatite nanorods on Ti shoul -> Ti implant surface carrying a hydroxyapatite nanor -> Hydrothermal growth of HA and Si-HA nanorod coatin -> Si is incorporated in the Si-HA nanorods at about  -> Si sits on phosphate sites as orthosilicate SiO4 4"
    },
    {
     "step": 2,
